# Findings that are true positives by pattern and non-secrets by meaning.
#
# One line per gitleaks fingerprint: commit:file:rule:line. An entry here is a
# claim that the value is public BY DESIGN, not that it is unimportant. Anything
# that is merely inconvenient to rotate does not belong in this file, it belongs
# in a rotation.
#
# Why this file exists at all: without it the finding fires on every push that
# touches the file, which teaches whoever is pushing to reach for
# GIT_ALLOW_CREDENTIAL_PUSH=1. A guard that is routinely overridden stops being a
# guard, and that is the path by which a real leak eventually gets waved through.

# Ahrefs Web Analytics site key, in the <script data-key=...> tag in the root
# layout. It is rendered into the HTML of every page and is readable by anyone
# who views source, so it is not a secret in any useful sense. It identifies the
# site for event ingestion and grants no read access to the Ahrefs account. The
# worst an attacker does with it is post junk pageviews into the analytics.
# Same class as the phc_ PostHog ingestion key, which is public for the same reason.
